Offline recording and synchronization

- Added a root-scoped Service Worker and installable app manifest. It caches the
  app shell and only the authenticated transaction-entry page; history and
  finance API responses are not cached. Signing out clears the cached entry
  page.
- Added IndexedDB storage for offline transactions. The entry form posts online
  through the existing authenticated transaction API and queues locally if the
  connection is unavailable or drops during submission.
- Captured the transaction's local date and a saved exchange-rate snapshot when
  queueing. Foreign-currency transactions without a saved quote are rejected
  from the offline queue rather than assigned a made-up rate.
- Added Background Sync where supported, with online-event and manual sync
  fallbacks. Sync obtains fresh authentication/CSRF context, only processes
  entries belonging to the currently signed-in user, and displays queued,
  synced, or conflict states.
- Reused server-side idempotency keys to make retries safe. The API accepts
  local transaction dates, rejects future dates, returns an existing posting
  for an identical retry, and reports a conflict when the same key is reused
  with different transaction data.
- Added an offline fallback screen and a visible queue with retry and review
  actions. Offline transaction entry is available after opening the entry page
  once online; locally stored financial data remains on the device until synced
  or dismissed.

